event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dev-dispatch-1.md\", \"content\": \"Dispatch for dev: implement \\\"greet, tested\\\"\\n\\nDeliver, in your repository clone, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `greet(\\\"Alice\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`).\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` with unit tests covering at least:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"Alice\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n3. Running `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` from the repo root must exit\\n   with status 0 (all tests pass).\\n\\nRequirements:\\n- Implement exactly this, nothing more (no extra CLI, no argparse, no unrelated\\n  files).\\n- Run the test command yourself before replying and confirm it exits 0.\\n- Commit your work to your own branch.\\n- Reply honestly with what you did, including the exact command you ran to\\n  verify tests pass and its result.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

